    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "For Sale by Private Treaty\r\n\r\nDennehy Auctioneers are delighted to present this rare and exciting opportunity to acquire a truly special historic seafront property, superbly positioned on the edge of Kinsale’s picturesque Inner Harbour. Comprising a two story residence over a basement, together with a spacious attic offering excellent potential for additional accommodation, this unique property represents an outstanding opportunity for those seeking to create a distinctive home in one of Cork’s most sought after coastal locations. The property also benefits from an over water decking area (currently in need of repair) with existing derricks providing potential for the launching of a punt or direct access to one’s own boat, together with a lower level courtyard garden. While requiring substantial renovation, the property offers enormous potential to restore, reimagine and transform it into a wonderful residence, tailored entirely to one’s own style and vision. A further significant benefit is the separate mid terrace stone built garage, complete with loft, located across from the main property. The garage offers potential for the creation of terraced gardens to the rear or possible conversion to off road parking, adding further versatility and appeal to this exceptional property.\r\n\r\nThe property’s unrivalled position is undoubtedly its greatest asset. Enjoying uninterrupted panoramic views across Kinsale Marina and the Inner Harbour, the outlook takes in the historic landmarks of James Fort and Charles Fort, together with the ever changing spectacle of life on the water. From the gentle movement of boats on moorings and the marina together with interesting wildlife to the activity of the vibrant harbour, the setting provides a captivating backdrop throughout the day and night and across the seasons. The over water decking and waterfront position further enhance the exceptional lifestyle on offer, providing a unique connection with the harbour and the opportunity to enjoy the water directly from the property. Perfectly positioned for enjoying all that Kinsale has to offer, the renowned Spaniard Inn and Man Friday Restaurant are just a one minute stroll away, while the vibrant heart of Kinsale town centre is within an easy 10 minute walk. The location effortlessly combines the charm and character of historic Kinsale with the exceptional lifestyle associated with waterfront living.\r\n\r\nOpportunities to acquire properties in such an exceptional seafront setting are seldom available. With its historic character, generous accommodation, outstanding views, waterfront access, garden courtyard and separate garage with further potential, this is a property that offers the discerning purchaser the chance to create something truly unique in one of Ireland’s most coveted coastal towns.\r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises of: Reception hall, large kitchen/dining room, large sunroom and balcony off. Ground floor with hallway, W.C., large sitting room, large sunroom off. Access to seafront patio and overwater deck. First floor with large bedroom (originally two separate bedrooms) and bathroom.\r\n\r\nFurther Details:\r\nCanopy over front porch.  Original front door with diamond lightwell over. Spacious landing/reception hall, cloaks. Cornicing. Stairs to first floor.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: 4.4 m x 6.4 m\r\nBuilt in fitted kitchen with single drainer stainless steel sink, eye level oven and dishwasher. Cornicing throughout. Double doors to sunroom.\r\n\r\n\r\nSunroom: 6.5 m x 2.2 m \r\nSunroom with stunning views over Kinsale harbour is of high quality timber construction and is double glazed throughout. French doors to balcony. Cast iron spiral staircase to lower level garden.\r\n\r\nFirst floor:\r\nLanding with pull down aluminium ladder to large attic.\r\n\r\nBedroom: 4.43 m x 5.86 m\r\nFitted wardrobes. Stunning panoramic views.\r\n\r\nBathroom: \r\nLarge bathroom with white suite of toilet, wash hand basin and pedestal. Bath with tiled surround and electric shower unit.\r\n\r\nBasement/Lower ground Floor: Hall with W.C. off, Large living room off.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 6.4m x 4.4m\r\nOpen fireplace with brick surround. Exposed beams. Door to Sunroom.\r\n\r\nLower sunroom: 6.5m x 2.2m\r\nSunroom with stunning views over Kinsale harbour is of high quality timber construction and is double glazed throughout. French doors to flagstone patio.\r\n\r\nOutside:\r\nProperty has an over water decking area (in need of repair) with derricks for the launching of a punt or direct access to one’s own boat. Lower level garden courtyard. Separate terraced stone built garage (with loft) (5.8 m x 3.6 m) located across from the main house with potential for further development or possible conversion to off road parking. At rear of garage is small yard and potential for terraced gardens.\r\n\r\nServices:\r\nMains water, mains sewer.\r\n\r\nTitle:\r\nGood marketable title.\r\n\r\n\r\nAll reasonable offers will be submitted to the vendor for consideration. These particulars have been prepared with care, but their accuracy is not guaranteed they do not form part of any contract and are not to be used in any legal action. Intending Purchasers/Lessees must satisfy themselves or otherwise of any statements contained herein and no warranty is implied in respect of the property described. The particulars are issued on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through this firm. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
